{"content":[{"c":["PARAPET*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Protective barrier around the circumference of house roofs. The parapet was required by the Law (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.22.8","r":"Deut.22.8","rawR":"Deut.22.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.22.8","value":"Deut.22.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 22:8"},") since flat roofs were widely used (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.2.6","r":"Josh.2.6","rawR":"Josh.2.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.2.6","value":"Josh.2.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 2:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.16.27","r":"Judg.16.27","rawR":"Judg.16.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.16.27","value":"Judg.16.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 16:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.9.25","r":"1Sam.9.25","rawR":"1Sam.9.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.9.25","value":"1Sam.9.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 9:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.22.1","r":"Isa.22.1","rawR":"Isa.22.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.22.1","value":"Isa.22.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 22:1"},"). Construction of a parapet would relieve the dweller from liability should a person fall from the roof."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Architecture"},"; ",{"href":"?item=HomesandDwellings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"HomesandDwellings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"HomesandDwellings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Homes and Dwellings"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Parapet","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 22:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.22.8","rawQueryValue":"Deut.22.8","sourceRefExact":"Deut.22.8"},{"anchorText":"Jos 2:6","canonicalizat